course: dictionary
lesson: 13062
title: Spotting pretending with feign
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To feign something is to pretend, so that people think you feel something or are ill, tired or asleep when you are not. Feign is a verb, so it changes: feign, feigns, feigned, feigning.
explain: «She feigned sleep so her brother would stop talking.» Her eyes were shut and her breathing was slow, but she was really awake. The word feigned tells you she was acting. Ask yourself: is the character truly feeling this, or only showing it?
explain: Stories often use feign to show a secret. A character may feign interest in a boring talk, or feign surprise at a gift they already knew about. The reader can see the gap between what the character shows and what they really feel.
explain: Phrases to know: feign illness, feign surprise, feign interest, feign sleep. Each one means pretending to feel or be something that is not true.
fact: Feign means to pretend, to act as if something is true when it is not.
fact: «Feigned» is the past tense: «He feigned surprise when he opened the present.»
fact: Animals can feign death to escape danger, lying still as if they were dead until the danger has gone.
fact: A good check is to swap in the words pretend to and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Feign is often used in stories to show that a character is acting, not really feeling something.
exercise: «She feigned sleep so her brother would stop talking.» What does feigned mean? | Snored loudly all night | *Pretended to be asleep when she was awake | Woke up early and ran outside | Fell asleep very quickly
exercise: «The fox began to feign death when the hunter came near.» What does feign mean here? | Sleep in a warm den | Hide its food for winter | *Pretend to be dead | Run as fast as it can
exercise: Tom wanted to be sent home early, so he feigned illness. Why did Tom feign illness? | To win a race at school | *To pretend he was ill when he was well | Because he was really ill and needed a doctor | To help his mum cook dinner
test: «He feigned surprise when his friends shouted, "Happy birthday!"» What does feigned surprise mean? | *Pretended to be surprised, though he already knew about the party | Was angry with his friends | Felt truly shocked by the noise | Was scared of the dark
test: Which phrase means pretending to be interested in something you find boring? | Feign death | Feign illness | *Feign interest | Feign sleep
exam: «The thief feigned tiredness to make the guard look away, then he ran.» What is the author telling us about the thief? | He was too scared to move | He was happy to be guarding the door | He was truly exhausted and had to rest | *He was acting tired, but he was not really tired
